<script>
import testRowsSource from 'crm/scripts/testRows.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
import Snippet from '#src/lib/Snippet.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="Report the CRM's test results one file at a time">
        <Snippet source={testRowsSource} path="scripts/testRows.ts" from={['await testRows(']} />

        <Code code={`bun scripts/testRows.ts --list
    bun scripts/testRows.ts --scope all --filter reports`} />

        <p><code>testRows</code> runs each test file of a <code>TestSuite</code> in a process of its
            own, and prints one <code>TestRow</code> per line as each file finishes, with a
            <code>TestCase</code> per test. A dashboard reads the rows as they land, rather than
            waiting on the whole run.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>What it does for the CRM</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>rowsCommand</code></td><td>the same command line for your own runner: <code>--list</code>, <code>--scope</code>, <code>--filter</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>RowItem</code> · <code>RowState</code></td><td>one entry a runner offers, and where it is in its run</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>inScope</code> · <code>matchesFilter</code></td><td>the selection, so a page filters with the function the runner selects with</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>A file whose runner wrote no report is <code>broken</code>, which is different from a
            red result: a suite that hangs reports nothing. One still running after ten minutes is
            stopped and reported <code>broken</code> too.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
